⍝ csubrank.apls -- Dyalog APL array form with the rank operator (2026).
⍝ (⍳nx)+⍤1⊢in adds the row-index vector to every row, then (⍳ny)+⍤0 1⊢
⍝ adds each iy to its own row, so no ny×nx index table is formed (compare
⍝ csubary.apls, in+(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx). The input is offset by 0.5 so it stays
⍝ floating point (see csubraw.apls). Run as
⍝    dyalogscript csubrank.apls 1000 2000 10
⎕IO←0
csub←{in nx ny←⍵ ⋄ (⍳ny)+⍤0 1⊢(⍳nx)+⍤1⊢in}
args←2⎕NQ#'GetCommandLineArgs'
(nrpt nx ny)←⍎¨¯3↑(1↓args),(0⌈4-≢args)↑'1000' '2000' '10'
in←0.5+(nx+ny)-(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx
⎕←'Arrays ',(⍕nx),' by ',(⍕ny),' count ',⍕nrpt
:For r :In ⍳nrpt
    out←csub in nx ny
:EndFor
:If ∨/,out≠in+(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx
    ⎕←'Error: result does not match'
:EndIf
